  "term": "scala media",
  "definition": "Scala media is the cochlear duct, an endolymph-filled spiral tube within the cochlea. It winds about 2.5 turns around the modiolus and separates the surrounding perilymph-filled canal into the scala vestibuli and scala tympani.",
